/* book exam traps: Mixing units inside a: σc in MPa and E in GPa gives a that is a thousand times wrong. Convert both to N/mm² first; a itself has no unit. | Using the true length L in λ instead of the effective length Le. Fixed-free, fixed-pinned and fixed-fixed ends all change Le and therefore λ (Euler buckling of columns and end conditions). | Feeding I into λ instead of r. λ = Le/r with r = √(I/A); I and r are linked by I = Ar², so one cannot stand in for r. | Getting PR larger than PE and accepting it. The formula is a reciprocal sum, so PR is always the smaller of the two loads — check it before writing the answer. */
